 # TODO(sloretz) Change to test_msgs_interfaces when ros2/rosidl_typesupport#120 is fixed
+# Local, rmw_tickle-specific patch (not upstream): rosidl_typesupport_tickle_c does not support
+# wstring at all, or an unbounded array with no explicit `# @capacity <N>` annotation (see test_
+# interface_files_rmw_tickle.patch's own UnboundedSequences.msg header comment for the array half's
+# full 'why', and rcl_interfaces_rmw_tickle.patch's own SetParameters.srv header comment for the
+# original, more detailed version of the same explanation - rmw_tickle/PLAN.md's Milestones 39/41/
+# 42/54 track the history) - exclude the test_interface_files messages that still hit either. Fixed
+# (`[N]`) and bounded (`[<=N]`) arrays of *any* element kind (POD, string, or nested message type)
+# were already fully supported even before this comment was last updated - `Arrays.msg`/`Bounded
+# Sequences.msg`/`BoundedPlainSequences.msg` (all fixed/bounded only, no unbounded arrays at all)
+# generate and compile cleanly with zero patch of their own needed, confirmed directly (Milestone
+# 55) - keeping them excluded here was itself stale, not a real gap; `UnboundedSequences.msg`
+# needed (and, via test_interface_files_rmw_tickle.patch, now has) explicit `# @capacity 3`
+# annotations on all 31 of its own unbounded array fields, matching its sibling `[3]`/`[<=3]` test
+# files' own element count for consistency. Un-excluding these three/four `.msg` files also
+# surfaced (and fixed, `ros2_adapter.py`) a real, previously-latent bug of its own: an IDL `char`
+# array's real ROS 2 struct member is `rosidl_runtime_c__uint8__Sequence`, not `..__char__
+# Sequence` (this generator's own converter was calling the wrong one - a hard compile error, not
+# silently wrong data, since `char[<=3] char_values` is one of `BoundedPlainSequences.msg`'s own
+# real fields) - see `ros2_adapter._ros2_sequence_scalar_type()`'s own doc comment for the full
+# story. `MultiNested.msg` stays excluded for a **different, genuine, structural reason, not a
+# generator gap**: its own worst-case wire size (six `[3]`/`[<=3]` fields, each nesting a full
+# `Arrays`/`BoundedSequences`/`UnboundedSequences` struct - already substantial structs in their
+# own right) exceeds `tt_MAX_BUFFER_LENGTH` (1472 bytes, `config.h`) outright, confirmed via a real
+# local compile hitting the generated `_Static_assert` for exactly this - TickLE's own single-
+# datagram design (DESIGN.md) has no fragmentation story, so no annotation choice can make this
+# message fit; a real, permanent limitation, tracked as such. Nested.msg itself (a single, same-
+# package `BasicTypes basic_types_value` field, no array involved) is NOT excluded either - rmw_
+# tickle/PLAN.md's Milestone 38 gave rosidl_typesupport_tickle_c exactly this shape (resolve.
+# Ros2Resolver's own "same-package sibling" case). Also drops ACTION/IDL files and the two action-
+# only entries below (msg/Builtins.msg, action/NestedMessage.action) - rmw_tickle has no action
+# support at all (see rmw_client.c/rmw_service.c). SRV_FILES is kept (rosidl_typesupport_tickle_cpp
+# now generates .srv typesupport too - rmw_tickle/PLAN.md's Milestone 11 row); BasicTypes.srv/
+# Empty.srv are both flat/plain-type and kept. `Arrays.srv` stays excluded too, but for a **third,
+# genuinely new kind of bug found this same pass (Milestone 55), unrelated to arrays or capacity at
+# all**: `test_msgs` also has both `msg/BasicTypes.msg` and `srv/BasicTypes.srv` - two *different*
+# interfaces sharing one base name - and this generator writes each one's own TickLE-side header to
+# a bare `BasicTypes.h` (in its own `msg/`/`srv/` output subdirectory respectively). `Arrays.srv`'s
+# own request nests the real `BasicTypes` *message*, but a bare `#include "BasicTypes.h"` from a
+# file living in `srv/` resolves via the C preprocessor's own same-directory-first quoted-include
+# search to `srv/BasicTypes.h` (`BasicTypesRequest`/`_Response`, from the unrelated *service*) -
+# not `msg/BasicTypes.h` (`BasicTypesData`, the one actually needed) - even though both directories
+# are on the real compile command's own `-I` list, confirmed via a real "incomplete element type
+# 'struct BasicTypesData'" compile error. A real same-package `.msg`/`.srv` base-name collision in
+# this generator's own header-naming convention, not anything Milestone 55 introduced - tracked as
+# a real follow-up (directory-qualified or ROS-name-qualified generated header names), not fixed in
+# this narrower pass; `Arrays.srv` itself doesn't need array-of-nested-type support at all (it's
+# fixed-`[3]`-only, same as `Arrays.msg`) - the collision is the entire and only reason it stays
+# excluded.
+list(FILTER test_interface_files_MSG_FILES EXCLUDE REGEX
+  ".*/(MultiNested|WStrings)\\.msg$")
+list(FILTER test_interface_files_SRV_FILES EXCLUDE REGEX ".*/Arrays\\.srv$")
 rosidl_generate_interfaces(test_msgs
   ${test_interface_files_MSG_FILES}
   ${test_interface_files_SRV_FILES}
-  ${test_interface_files_ACTION_FILES}
-  ${test_interface_files_IDL_FILES}
-  "msg/Builtins.msg"
-  "action/NestedMessage.action"
   DEPENDENCIES builtin_interfaces
   ADD_LINTER_TESTS
 )
